    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 the only test class in the project). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated logger named `NOTIFY`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger notifyLogger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. In `addOwner`, after the owner is persisted (so its `memberId` is populated by `saveOwner`) and after the existing audit events, emit the welcome line carrying the owner id and memberId:\n   ```java\n   notifyLogger.info(\"welcome: owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThis runs only on the successful create path (after the quota/duplicate rejections return early), matching the spec. The `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the memberId read back from `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 passes, as does the full suite.",
